window.DOCS["6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e"]={"id":"6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e","summary":{"title_zh":"遺傳資源數位序列資訊","what":"這是第一工作小組主席提出的決議草案（工作小組會議室文件 CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19，多處文字仍在方括號內，尚未定案）。內容涉及遺傳資源數位序列資訊（DSI）之多邊機制，包括卡利基金（Cali Fund）之營運、貢獻、分配、治理與審查，以落實DSI使用後之利益分享。","points":["決定設立視資源可用性而定之特設開放式工作小組，進一步發展包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，並於第十八次締約方大會提出建議（第3段）。","重申大型實體將依決定16/2貢獻，中小型實體則不預期貢獻但獲鼓勵（第5段）；重申1%利潤或0.1%營收之貢獻率僅為指示性（第7段）；門檻應適用於不受他人控制之最高層法人（第6段）；決定於第十八次締約方大會對多邊機制之首次審查中檢討門檻與安排（第8段）。","呼籲在商業活動中直接或間接使用DSI之部門中的使用者，依決定16/2與第6段，就其利潤或營收之一定比例貢獻予卡利基金（第9段）。","承認使用者之潛在不對等，包括有限或初步使用DSI之使用者（第10段）。","要求執行秘書在資源許可下委託研究潛在之額外模式（包括依產品或服務組合計算之貢獻途徑，特別適用於有限或初步使用者），並交付同行審查，提交特設開放式工作小組審議（第12段）；並邀請各方與利害關係人（特別是私部門）就此提交意見與資料（第11段）。","邀請各方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區及利害關係人，就「實體」與「DSI之直接與間接使用」等用語之必要性、範圍與定義提出意見與資料；並要求執行秘書彙整（第14至15段）。","承認卡利基金證書（僅適用於多邊機制範圍內之DSI）可能提供法律確定性與可預測性，並可作為激勵使用者貢獻之重要方式之一（第16段）；注意到指導委員會之證書工作，並邀請其續行，以語言、法律效力與範圍、發行程序與查核為優先（第18段）。","支持指導委員會作為例外措施發出年度過渡性證書，以激勵對卡利基金之貢獻，並為第十八次締約方大會檢討機制累積經驗（第21段）。","要求締約方提交資訊，並要求執行秘書彙整後提供指導委員會（第19至20段）；注意到依透明與問責原則，證書持有者名單將由多邊機制秘書處公開（第22段）。","歡迎特設技術專家小組（分配方法）之工作成果，並注意到分配設計原則（公平性、效率、透明與信任）（第23至24段）。","決定設立視資源可用性而定之特設技術專家小組，就分配方法進行工作，包括發展針對原住民族與地方社區之分配方法，並向特設開放式工作小組報告（第30段）；為確保能向原住民族與地方社區撥付資金，指導委員會之提案應依國情與國內法，考慮透過政府機關、原住民族與地方社區自行指定之機構直接撥付、國家層級指定實體，或混合或因地制宜之安排（第31段）。","在非金錢利益分享方面，承認仍需進一步工作並需充足資金（第32段）；要求執行秘書邀請各方提交意見，並委託研究當前非金錢利益分享之現況與能力缺口、成功案例、與其他國際協定之比較，以及將其納入綱要監測架構之方式（第33(a)至(c)段）。","歡迎指導委員會成員規則與交錯換屆之過渡安排（第39段）；要求指導委員會於其議事規則中增加成員遴選條款，由區域群組與選區提名（第40段）；要求執行秘書邀請各區域提名一名代表（第41段）。","回顧多邊機制（含卡利基金）於締約方大會之權威與指導下運作並向其負責（第44段）；注意到卡利基金目前由聯合國多方伙伴信託基金辦公室管理（第45段）；認為諒解備忘錄應與決定16/2及15/9一致（第49段）；呼籲諒解備忘錄簽署方將用語由捐助者／捐款改為貢獻者／貢獻（第50段）；並注意到指導委員會直至諒解備忘錄簽署後才首次召開（第51段）。","承認多邊機制（含卡利基金）將於第十八次締約方大會接受審查，其審查包括治理，含諒解備忘錄、附件與指導委員會之職權範圍與操作程序（第48段）；認為在目前草擬之諒解備忘錄下，其仍將繼續適用（第55段）；並決定指導委員會得修改諒解備忘錄以外之營運文件，但不改變決定16/2所定之治理安排（第56段）。","決定實施審查方法（第57段）；要求執行秘書發展並散布調查、委託審查報告（第58段）；邀請相關行動者回應調查（第59段）；要求工作小組審議報告與指導委員會之意見（第60段）。","呼籲有使用者之締約方採取措施，確保使用者依多邊機制之模式貢獻（第61段）；呼籲締約方，並邀請其他政府與相關組織，組織參與性活動與伙伴關係，以鼓勵私部門參與（第62段）。","要求執行秘書加強與其他相關國際組織之合作，包括《糧食與農業植物遺傳資源國際條約》、世界衛生組織、世界智慧財產權組織，以及BBNJ協定（第64段）。"],"open":["序言中關於各國對其自然資源之主權權利、及多邊機制須尊重國家取得與利益分享法律之段落，以及其替代文字（alt），仍未定案。","第17段：限定僅金錢貢獻且達第7段費率者方可獲發證書之「只有」一詞，仍未定案。","第25段（整段）：指導委員會於第十八次締約方大會採用分配方法前，以例外方式分配資金之授權，以及以2億或1.5億美元資本化為條件之文字，仍未定案。","第25(a)段：分配比例仍有多種選項，包括平均分配（25%或20%）、依GNI調整（25%、10%或20%）、依全球環境基金生物多樣性效益指數分配（50%、70%或60%）。","第25(b)段：原住民族與地方社區分配中，開發中國家（90%）與已開發國家（10%）之比例及其安排文字，仍未定案。","第26段（整段）：依最終分配方法調整已分配金額之文字，仍未定案；第28段所引用之第25段分配方法因此亦未定案。","第34至35段（資料公開與問責）：英文原稿中僅見結束括號位於第35段，段落之地位仍未定案。","第52段（整段）：設立法律專家小組（每一聯合國區域一名成員及一名原住民族與地方社區代表）、其任務、是否加入企業界觀察員之文字，以及對諒解備忘錄之修訂，仍未定案。","第54(d)段：將報告與指導委員會檢視結果提交特設開放式工作小組，並向第十八次締約方大會提出建議之文字，仍未定案。","第63段：支持指導委員會與秘書處之工作之括號文字（包括能力建構、技術協助、提高認知與資訊分享之措辭），仍未定案。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p001.md","en":"                                                                                      CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n                                                                                   Distr.: Limited\n                                                                                   29 October 2026\n                                                                                   Original: English\n\n\n\n\nConference of the Parties to the\nConvention on Biological Diversity\nSeventeenth meeting\nYerevan, 19–30 October 2026\nAgenda item 11\nDigital sequence information on genetic resources\nWorking Group I\n\n       Digital sequence information on genetic resources*\n       Draft decision submitted by the Chair of Working Group I\n\n               The Conference of the Parties,\n               Recalling decisions 15/9 of 19 December 2022 and 16/2 of 1 November 2024,\n             [Reaffirming the sovereign rights of States over their natural resources, and emphasizing that\n       the operationalization of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, must respect\n       applicable national access and benefit-sharing legislation and mutually agreed terms, while\n       preserving the balance established by decision 16/2;]\n              alt Recognizing that the approach to the fair and equitable benefit-sharing from the use of DSI\n       set out in the present decision is without prejudice to national ABS measures and does not affect the\n       rights and obligations of any Party deriving from any existing international agreement;\n              Emphasizing the importance of preserving the distinctive nature of the Cali Fund as a benefit\n       sharing fund, ensuring transparency and accountability, and maintaining clear governance structures,\n       institutional mandates, responsibilities and decision-making authority consistent with decision 16/2;\n              1.     Expresses its appreciation to the Governments of Germany, Norway and the United\n       Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland and to the European Union for their generous\n       financial support for the activities linked with the operationalization of the Multilateral Mechanism\n       for the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits from the Use of Digital Sequence Information on\n       Genetic Resources, including the Cali Fund, and to the Governments of Germany and South Africa\n       for hosting the second and third meetings of the Steering Committee, respectively;\n            2.    Takes note with appreciation of the report of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral\n       Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;1\n              3.    Decides to establish, subject to the availability of resources, an ad hoc open-ended\n       working group on benefit-sharing from the use of digital sequence information on genetic resources\n       to further develop the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, to consider, inter alia, the\n       issues pursuant to this decision as noted in the relevant paragraphs of this document, and to make\n       recommendations to the Conference of the Parties for consideration at its eighteenth meeting;\n\n\n* The present document is being issued without formal editing.\n1 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1.","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n分發：限閱\n2026年10月29日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19<br />\n分發：限閱<br />\n2026年10月29日<br />\n原文：英文</p>"},{"md":"生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19日至30日\n議程項目 11\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19日至30日<br />\n議程項目 11<br />\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊<br />\n第一工作小組</p>"},{"md":"遺傳資源數位序列資訊*\n由第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>遺傳資源數位序列資訊*<br />\n由第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案<br />\n締約方大會，</p>"},{"md":"**回顧** 2022年12月19日之決議 15/9 及 2024年11月1日之決議 16/2，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong> 2022年12月19日之決議 15/9 及 2024年11月1日之決議 16/2，</p>"},{"md":"[**重申** 各國對其自然資源擁有主權，並**強調**包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制的操作化，必須尊重適用的國家取得與利益分享立法及共同商定條件，同時維持決議 16/2 所建立之平衡；]","html":"<p>[<strong>重申</strong> 各國對其自然資源擁有主權，並<strong>強調</strong>包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制的操作化，必須尊重適用的國家取得與利益分享立法及共同商定條件，同時維持決議 16/2 所建立之平衡；]</p>"},{"md":"替代方案：**認識到** 本決議所設定之關於使用 DSI 達成公平且公正之利益分享方式，不損及國家取得與利益分享（ABS）措施，且不影響任何締約方因現有國際協議而產生之權利與義務；","html":"<p>替代方案：<strong>認識到</strong> 本決議所設定之關於使用 DSI 達成公平且公正之利益分享方式，不損及國家取得與利益分享（ABS）措施，且不影響任何締約方因現有國際協議而產生之權利與義務；</p>"},{"md":"**強調** 維持卡利基金作為利益分享基金之獨特性、確保透明度與問責制，並維持與決議 16/2 一致之清晰治理結構、機構職能、責任與決策權之重要性；","html":"<p><strong>強調</strong> 維持卡利基金作為利益分享基金之獨特性、確保透明度與問責制，並維持與決議 16/2 一致之清晰治理結構、機構職能、責任與決策權之重要性；</p>"},{"md":"1. **對** 德國、挪威、大不列顛及北愛爾蘭聯合王國政府以及歐盟為與「使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊公平且公正分享利益之多邊機制」（包括卡利基金）操作化相關活動所提供之慷慨財務支持，以及對德國與南非政府分別主辦指導委員會第二及第三次會議，表示感謝；","html":"<p>1. <strong>對</strong> 德國、挪威、大不列顛及北愛爾蘭聯合王國政府以及歐盟為與「使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊公平且公正分享利益之多邊機制」（包括卡利基金）操作化相關活動所提供之慷慨財務支持，以及對德國與南非政府分別主辦指導委員會第二及第三次會議，表示感謝；</p>"},{"md":"2. **贊同地注意到** 卡利基金多邊機制指導委員會之報告；¹","html":"<p>2. <strong>贊同地注意到</strong> 卡利基金多邊機制指導委員會之報告；¹</p>"},{"md":"3. **決定** 在資源可用的情況下，成立一個關於使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益分享特設開放式工作小組，以進一步發展包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，並於其中考慮本文件相關段落所述之依據本決議所生之議題，並向締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十八次會議審議；","html":"<p>3. <strong>決定</strong> 在資源可用的情況下，成立一個關於使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益分享特設開放式工作小組，以進一步發展包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，並於其中考慮本文件相關段落所述之依據本決議所生之議題，並向締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十八次會議審議；</p>"},{"md":"* 本文件目前未經正式編輯。\n¹ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1.","html":"<ul>\n<li>本文件目前未經正式編輯。<br />\n¹ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1.</li>\n</ul>"}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p002.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n\n\n       I\n       Operations of the Cali Fund\nThresholds and contribution rates\n              4.     Takes note of the study on contribution rates, including implications for revenue\n       generation and economic competitiveness, and on national and international standards for the\n       identification of small, medium and large entities;2\n              5.     Recognizes that thresholds for identifying small, medium and large entities vary among\n       jurisdictions and reaffirms that large entities will contribute to the global fund in accordance with\n       decision 16/2; also considers that entities classified as small or medium enterprises in national\n       jurisdictions, or those below the thresholds set out in paragraph 3 of the annex to decision 16/2, are\n       not expected to contribute to the Cali Fund but are encouraged to do so;\n             6.    Affirms that the thresholds should be applied at the level of the highest legal entity in\n       the ownership chain, where that entity is not itself controlled by another;\n             7.   Reaffirms that the contribution rates of 1 per cent of the profits or 0.1 per cent of the\n       revenue of the contributing entities using digital sequence information under the Multilateral\n       Mechanism, are indicative;\n              8.     Decides that the thresholds and arrangements referred to in paragraph 6 and the\n       indicatives rates referred to in paragraph 7 are reviewed as part of the first review of the Multilateral\n       Mechanism including the Cali Fund at the eighteen meeting of the Conference of the Parties in light\n       of the outcomes of the work under paragraphs 11 and 12 below taking into account the need to ensure\n       adequate and predictable contributions to the Cali Fund;\n              9.     Calls upon users of digital sequence information on genetic resources in sectors that\n       directly or indirectly benefit from its use in their commercial activities to contribute a proportion of\n       their profits or revenue to the Cali Fund, in accordance with decision 16/2 and paragraph 6 above,\n       without prejudice to applicable national access and benefit sharing legislation and obligations;\nPotential additional modalities\n               10. Recognizes the potential asymmetries among users, including those making limited or\n       initial use of digital sequence information on genetic resources;\n             11      Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and\n       relevant organizations and stakeholders, in particular the private sector, to submit views and\n       information on the potential value of additional modalities, including a proportionate contribution\n       pathways such as a products- and services-based modality for but not limited to entities making\n       limited or initial use of digital sequence information on genetic resources in the context of the\n       potential for entities to calculate their contributions to the Cali Fund, based on their use of digital\n       sequence information on genetic resources within the scope of the Multilateral Mechanism, that could\n       complement or refine the approach established in decision 16/2;\n             12. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to commission\n       a study on potential additional modalities to explore potential proportionate contribution pathways,\n       including for entities making limited or initial use of digital sequence information on genetic\n       resources to enable entities to calculate their contributions to the Fund on the basis of the products\n       or services in their portfolios developed using digital sequence information on genetic resources\n       within the scope of the Multilateral Mechanism, and to analyse and evaluate the feasibility,\n       practicality, efficiency and legal and technical challenges of those pathways, including equity\n       implications, to subject the study to peer review, and to make it available to the ad hoc open-ended\n\n2 CBD/COP/17/INF/18\n\n\n\n2/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"I\n卡利基金之運作\n門檻與貢獻率\n4.\n**注意到**關於貢獻率（包括對收益產生與經濟競爭力的影響），以及關於識別小型、中型與大型實體之國家與國際標準的研究；2\n5.\n**承認**識別小型、中型與大型實體的門檻因司法管轄區而異，並**重申**大型實體應根據決議 16/2 向全球基金進行貢獻；亦**考慮到**在國家司法管轄區內被歸類為中小企業，或低於決議 16/2 附件第 3 段所列門檻之實體，不被預期需向卡利基金進行貢獻，但鼓勵其進行貢獻；\n6.\n**確認**門檻應適用於所有權鏈中最高層級之法律實體，且該實體本身不受其他實體控制；\n7.\n**重申**在多邊機制下使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻實體，其貢獻率為利潤之 1% 或營收之 0.1%，僅具指標性；\n8.\n**決定**第 6 段所述之門檻與安排，以及第 7 段所述之指標性稅率，應作為包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制第一次審查的一部分，於第十八次締約方大會進行審查，並應根據下文第 11 段與第 12 段工作之結果，並考量確保對卡利基金有充足且可預測之貢獻之必要性；\n9.\n**呼籲**在商業活動中直接或間接從使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊中獲益之產業領域內，遺傳資源數位序列資訊的使用者，應根據決議 16/2 及上述第 6 段，將其利潤或營收之比例捐獻至卡利基金，且不損害適用之國家取得與利益分享立法及義務；","html":"<p>I<br />\n卡利基金之運作<br />\n門檻與貢獻率<br />\n4.<br />\n<strong>注意到</strong>關於貢獻率（包括對收益產生與經濟競爭力的影響），以及關於識別小型、中型與大型實體之國家與國際標準的研究；2<br />\n5.<br />\n<strong>承認</strong>識別小型、中型與大型實體的門檻因司法管轄區而異，並<strong>重申</strong>大型實體應根據決議 16/2 向全球基金進行貢獻；亦<strong>考慮到</strong>在國家司法管轄區內被歸類為中小企業，或低於決議 16/2 附件第 3 段所列門檻之實體，不被預期需向卡利基金進行貢獻，但鼓勵其進行貢獻；<br />\n6.<br />\n<strong>確認</strong>門檻應適用於所有權鏈中最高層級之法律實體，且該實體本身不受其他實體控制；<br />\n7.<br />\n<strong>重申</strong>在多邊機制下使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻實體，其貢獻率為利潤之 1% 或營收之 0.1%，僅具指標性；<br />\n8.<br />\n<strong>決定</strong>第 6 段所述之門檻與安排，以及第 7 段所述之指標性稅率，應作為包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制第一次審查的一部分，於第十八次締約方大會進行審查，並應根據下文第 11 段與第 12 段工作之結果，並考量確保對卡利基金有充足且可預測之貢獻之必要性；<br />\n9.<br />\n<strong>呼籲</strong>在商業活動中直接或間接從使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊中獲益之產業領域內，遺傳資源數位序列資訊的使用者，應根據決議 16/2 及上述第 6 段，將其利潤或營收之比例捐獻至卡利基金，且不損害適用之國家取得與利益分享立法及義務；</p>"},{"md":"潛在之額外模式\n10. **承認**使用者之間存在潛在的不對稱性，包括對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之使用者；\n11. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人（特別是私營部門），就額外模式之潛在價值提交意見與資訊，包括比例貢獻路徑，例如針對（但不限於）在多邊機制範圍內對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之實體，採取以產品與服務為基礎之模式，其背景為實體可根據其在多邊機制範圍內對遺傳資源數位序列資訊之使用，計算其對卡利基金之貢獻，且該模式可補充或完善決議 16/2 所建立之方法；\n12. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，委託進行一項關於潛在額外模式的研究，以探索潛在的比例貢獻路徑，包括針對對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之實體，使實體能夠根據其在多邊機制範圍內使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊所開發之產品或服務組合，計算其對基金之貢獻，並分析與評估該等路徑之可行性、實務性、效率以及法律與技術挑戰（包括公平性影響），並將該研究提交同儕審查，並提供予特設開放式工作小組，","html":"<p>潛在之額外模式<br />\n10. <strong>承認</strong>使用者之間存在潛在的不對稱性，包括對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之使用者；<br />\n11. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人（特別是私營部門），就額外模式之潛在價值提交意見與資訊，包括比例貢獻路徑，例如針對（但不限於）在多邊機制範圍內對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之實體，採取以產品與服務為基礎之模式，其背景為實體可根據其在多邊機制範圍內對遺傳資源數位序列資訊之使用，計算其對卡利基金之貢獻，且該模式可補充或完善決議 16/2 所建立之方法；<br />\n12. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，委託進行一項關於潛在額外模式的研究，以探索潛在的比例貢獻路徑，包括針對對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之實體，使實體能夠根據其在多邊機制範圍內使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊所開發之產品或服務組合，計算其對基金之貢獻，並分析與評估該等路徑之可行性、實務性、效率以及法律與技術挑戰（包括公平性影響），並將該研究提交同儕審查，並提供予特設開放式工作小組，</p>"},{"md":"2 CBD/COP/17/INF/18","html":"<p>2 CBD/COP/17/INF/18</p>"},{"md":"2/11","html":"<p>2/11</p>"}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p003.md","en":"                                                                                   CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n       working group for its consideration as a complement or refinement of the approach established in\n       decision 16/2;\n            13. Decides to adopt of appropriate, if any, additional modalities, including as described in\n      paragraph 12 above, at the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\nDefinitions\n             14    Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and\n      relevant organizations and stakeholders, in particular the private sector and the scientific community,\n      to submit their views and information on the need, scope and/or definition of the terms ‘entity’,\n      “direct and indirect use of digital sequence information on genetic resources” and any possible\n      options in the context of the operationalization of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali\n      Fund;\n               15    Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to:\n               (a)   Compile and synthesize the submissions pursuant to paragraph 13;\n            (b) Make the synthesis available to the ad hoc open-ended working group for its\n      consideration;\nCertificates\n            16. Recognizes that Cali Fund certificates, as applied solely to the digital sequence\n      information within the scope of the Multilateral Mechanism, has links with some of its other\n      modalities, may provide legal certainty and predictability to entities and will be one of the important\n      means to incentivise, and encourage users to contribute to the global fund in line with the modalities\n      of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, while recalling that every monetary\n      contribution to the Cali Fund will be acknowledged by a receipt as evidence of the financial\n      transaction;\n             17. Clarifies that [only] monetary contributions made by users at or above the rates referred\n      to in paragraph 7 above will entitle users to receive a Cali Fund certificate for the year to which the\n      contribution relates, without prejudice to possible future modalities;\n             18. Takes note of the work of the Steering Committee on certificates, in particular in relation\n      to paragraphs 15 and 26 of the annex to decision 16/2, and invites the Committee to further work on\n      the topic, as a priority, focusing on the language, legal effect and scope, issuance process and\n      verification of the certificates, taking into account the criteria in paragraphs 9 and 10 of\n      decision 15/9, with a view to promote legal certainty to both Parties and contributing users of the\n      digital sequence information on genetic resources;\n             19. Requests Parties, while recalling paragraph 13 of the annex to decision 16/2, 16/2, to\n      submit information, to be presented to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting by the\n      Steering Committee, on the characteristics and elements that a Cali Fund certificate would need to\n      operationalize paragraph 15 of the annex to decision 16/2, and the processes, if any, that would need\n      to be undertaken at the national level to recognize or give legal effect to such certificates, including\n      in their national legislation;\n              20. Requests the Executive Secretary to compile the information submitted pursuant to\n      paragraph 19 above and provide it to the Steering Committee for its information and so that it may\n      take it into account in their work on the certificates and report on it to the Conference of the Parties\n      at its eighteenth meeting;\n             21. Supports the Steering Committee to issue annual interim certificates, resulting from the\n      work noted in paragraph 18 above for applicable contributions to the Cali Fund, including current\n      ones, as an exceptional measure to incentivize contributions to the Cali Fund, and to build experience\n      and lessons learned to be considered as part of its review of the Mechanism by the Conference of the\n      Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n\n                                                                                                         3/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"作為對決議 16/2 所建立之方法的補充或完善，供工作小組審議；\n13. **決定**於第十八次締約方大會，採納適當的（若有）額外作業模式，包括如上述第 12 段所述之內容；","html":"<p>作為對決議 16/2 所建立之方法的補充或完善，供工作小組審議；<br />\n13. <strong>決定</strong>於第十八次締約方大會，採納適當的（若有）額外作業模式，包括如上述第 12 段所述之內容；</p>"},{"md":"定義","html":"<p>定義</p>","pre":"，包括如上述第 12 段所述之內容；\n\n"},{"md":"14. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，特別是私營部門與科學界，就「實體」、「遺傳資源數位序列資訊之直接與間接利用」之必要性、範圍及／或定義，以及在多邊機制（包括卡利基金）運作化背景下之任何可能選項，提交其觀點與資訊；","html":"<p>14. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，特別是私營部門與科學界，就「實體」、「遺傳資源數位序列資訊之直接與間接利用」之必要性、範圍及／或定義，以及在多邊機制（包括卡利基金）運作化背景下之任何可能選項，提交其觀點與資訊；</p>"},{"md":"15. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>15. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 編纂並綜合根據第 13 段所提交之內容；","html":"<p>(a) 編纂並綜合根據第 13 段所提交之內容；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 將綜合報告提供予特設開放式工作小組審議；","html":"<p>(b) 將綜合報告提供予特設開放式工作小組審議；</p>"},{"md":"證明書","html":"<p>證明書</p>","pre":"合報告提供予特設開放式工作小組審議；\n\n"},{"md":"16. **認可**卡利基金證明書（僅適用於多邊機制範圍內之數位序列資訊）與其其他部分作業模式有關聯，可為實體提供法律確定性與可預測性，且將是激勵並鼓勵使用者根據多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之作業模式向全球基金做出貢獻的重要手段之一；同時**回顧**向卡利基金進行的每一筆金錢貢獻都將透過收據予以確認，作為財務交易之證明；","html":"<p>16. <strong>認可</strong>卡利基金證明書（僅適用於多邊機制範圍內之數位序列資訊）與其其他部分作業模式有關聯，可為實體提供法律確定性與可預測性，且將是激勵並鼓勵使用者根據多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之作業模式向全球基金做出貢獻的重要手段之一；同時<strong>回顧</strong>向卡利基金進行的每一筆金錢貢獻都將透過收據予以確認，作為財務交易之證明；</p>"},{"md":"17. **澄清**，在不影響未來可能之作業模式之前提下，[僅]由使用者以高於或等於上述第 7 段所述之費率所進行的金錢貢獻，將使該使用者有權獲得與該貢獻所屬年度相對應之卡利基金證明書；","html":"<p>17. <strong>澄清</strong>，在不影響未來可能之作業模式之前提下，[僅]由使用者以高於或等於上述第 7 段所述之費率所進行的金錢貢獻，將使該使用者有權獲得與該貢獻所屬年度相對應之卡利基金證明書；</p>"},{"md":"18. **注意到**指導委員會關於證明書之工作，特別是關於決議 16/2 附件第 15 段與第 26 段之工作，並**邀請**委員會將此議題作為優先事項進行進一步工作，重點關注證明書之用語、法律效力與範圍、核發程序及驗證，並考量決議 15/9 第 9 段與第 10 段之標準，旨在為締約方以及遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻使用者促進法律確定性；","html":"<p>18. <strong>注意到</strong>指導委員會關於證明書之工作，特別是關於決議 16/2 附件第 15 段與第 26 段之工作，並<strong>邀請</strong>委員會將此議題作為優先事項進行進一步工作，重點關注證明書之用語、法律效力與範圍、核發程序及驗證，並考量決議 15/9 第 9 段與第 10 段之標準，旨在為締約方以及遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻使用者促進法律確定性；</p>"},{"md":"19. **請求**締約方（同時**回顧**決議 16/2 附件第 13 段）提交資訊，由指導委員會於第十八次締約方大會提交，內容應關於卡利基金證明書為使決議 16/2 附件第 15 段得以運作化所需之特性與要素，以及在國家層級（包括在其國內立法中）為承認或賦予此類證明書法律效力而需要進行之程序（若有）；","html":"<p>19. <strong>請求</strong>締約方（同時<strong>回顧</strong>決議 16/2 附件第 13 段）提交資訊，由指導委員會於第十八次締約方大會提交，內容應關於卡利基金證明書為使決議 16/2 附件第 15 段得以運作化所需之特性與要素，以及在國家層級（包括在其國內立法中）為承認或賦予此類證明書法律效力而需要進行之程序（若有）；</p>"},{"md":"20. **請求**執行秘書編纂根據上述第 19 段所提交之資訊，並提供予指導委員會以供其參考，以便其在關於證明書的工作中將其納入考量，並於第十八次締約方大會向締約方大會報告；","html":"<p>20. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書編纂根據上述第 19 段所提交之資訊，並提供予指導委員會以供其參考，以便其在關於證明書的工作中將其納入考量，並於第十八次締約方大會向締約方大會報告；</p>"},{"md":"21. **支持**指導委員會針對適用於卡利基金之貢獻（包括目前的貢獻），根據上述第 18 段所載之工作，核發年度臨時證明書，作為激勵卡利基金貢獻之特殊措施，並藉此累積經驗與教訓，以作為締約方於第十八次締約方大會對機制進行審查時之考量部分。","html":"<p>21. <strong>支持</strong>指導委員會針對適用於卡利基金之貢獻（包括目前的貢獻），根據上述第 18 段所載之工作，核發年度臨時證明書，作為激勵卡利基金貢獻之特殊措施，並藉此累積經驗與教訓，以作為締約方於第十八次締約方大會對機制進行審查時之考量部分。</p>"}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p004.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n             22. Notes that, in line with the principle of transparency and accountability of the\n       Multilateral Mechanism, the list of Cali Fund certificates and their recipients will be made public by\n       the Secretariat of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;\nAllocation methodology\n             23. Welcomes the outcomes of the work of the of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on\n       Allocation Methodology on the disbursement of funds from the Cali Fund;3\n              24.   Takes note of the design principles for the allocation formula and its future revisions,\n       guided by decision 16/2, namely equity, fairness and impact; efficiency; transparency and\n       confidence; and recognizes that the methodology should reflect the contributions to conservation and\n       sustainable use of indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth within\n       those communities;\n             25. [Authorizes the Steering Committee, on an exceptional basis, to allocate funding from\n       the Cali Fund on an exceptional basis before the allocation methodology is adopted at the eighteenth\n       meeting of the Conference of the Parties provided that capitalization reaches [200][150] million\n       United States Dollars, in accordance with the following provisions, which shall cease to apply upon\n       the conclusion of that meeting, without prejudice to the allocation methodology to be adopted therein:\n             (a) Among developing country Parties, in accordance with paragraphs 18 and 20 of the\n       annex to decision 16/2:\n             (i)     [25%][20%] allocated equally among all countries;\n             (ii)    [25%][10%][20%] allocated according to GNI per capita adjusted by the factors used in\n                     the United Nations scale of assessments formula; countries with lower adjusted GNI per\n                     capita will receive higher allocations;\n             (iii)   [50%][70%][60%] allocated according to the Benefits Index for Biodiversity as\n                     employed by the Global Environment Facility (updated data from the ninth\n                     replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, at the global\n                     level);\n              (b) Among indigenous peoples and local communities, [90%] of their allocation is reserved\n       for indigenous peoples and local communities in developing countries, allocated among countries\n       according to paragraph 25 (a) above, and [10%] of their allocation is reserved for indigenous peoples\n       and local communities in developed countries. [Within these allocations, funds may be disbursed\n       according to the self-identified priorities of indigenous peoples and local communities in line with\n       and subject to the arrangements set out in the annex to decision 16/2;]\n             26. [Decides that allocation made under the agreed methodologies shall be subject to\n       adjustment, as appropriate, following the adoption of the final allocation methodology by eighteenth\n       meeting of the Conference of the Parties to ensure consistency with final methodology;]\n             27. Emphasizes that the allocation methodology will evolve over time as additional and new\n       information becomes available, and recognizes that the methodology requires further technical\n       development and refinement in accordance with the recommendations of the Ad Hoc Technical\n       Expert Group on Allocation Methodology;\n             28. Requests the Steering Committee to apply the allocation methodology as outlined in\n       paragraph 25, without prejudging its refinement at the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth\n       meeting;\n             29.      Invites Parties to submit views on the report of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group as\n       well as the allocation methodology as outlined in paragraph 25;\n\n\n3 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.\n\n\n\n4/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"22. **注意到**，為符合多邊機制透明與問責之原則，卡利基金證明書及其受款人名單將由多邊機制秘書處（包括卡利基金秘書處）公開；","html":"<p>22. <strong>注意到</strong>，為符合多邊機制透明與問責之原則，卡利基金證明書及其受款人名單將由多邊機制秘書處（包括卡利基金秘書處）公開；</p>"},{"md":"分配方法論","html":"<p>分配方法論</p>","pre":"制秘書處（包括卡利基金秘書處）公開；\n\n"},{"md":"23. **歡迎**分配方法論特設技術專家小組關於卡利基金資金撥付工作成果之結果；³","html":"<p>23. <strong>歡迎</strong>分配方法論特設技術專家小組關於卡利基金資金撥付工作成果之結果；³</p>"},{"md":"24. **注意到**以決議 16/2 為指引，分配公式之設計原則及其未來修訂原則，即：公平、公正與影響；效率；透明與信心；並**承認**該方法論應反映原住民族與地方社區（包括該社群內之女性與青年）對保育與永續利用之貢獻；","html":"<p>24. <strong>注意到</strong>以決議 16/2 為指引，分配公式之設計原則及其未來修訂原則，即：公平、公正與影響；效率；透明與信心；並<strong>承認</strong>該方法論應反映原住民族與地方社區（包括該社群內之女性與青年）對保育與永續利用之貢獻；</p>"},{"md":"25. [**授權**指導委員會，在例外情況下，於第十八次締約方大會通過分配方法論之前，在資本額達到 [200][150] 百萬美元的前提下，依據下列規定例外地從卡利基金撥付資金，該規定於該次會議結束時應停止適用，且不影響屆時將採納之分配方法論：\n(a) 在開發中國家締約方之間，依據決議 16/2 附件第 18 段與第 20 段：\n(i) [25%][20%] 平等分配予所有國家；\n(ii) [25%][10%][20%] 依據經聯合國攤款比例公式所用因子調整後之每人國民總所得（GNI）進行分配；經調整後之每人 GNI 較低之國家將獲得較高分配；\n(iii) [50%][70%][60%] 依據全球環境基金所採用之生物多樣性利益指數（更新自全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間之全球層級資料）進行分配；\n(b) 在原住民族與地方社區之間，其分配額之 [90%] 預留予開發中國家之原住民族與地方社區，並依上述第 25 (a) 段於各國間進行分配，其分配額之 [10%] 預留予已開發國家之原住民族與地方社區。[在這些分配額中，資金得根據原住民族與地方社區自我認定的優先事項進行撥付，但須符合並受決議 16/2 附件所列安排之約束；]","html":"<p>25. [<strong>授權</strong>指導委員會，在例外情況下，於第十八次締約方大會通過分配方法論之前，在資本額達到 [200][150] 百萬美元的前提下，依據下列規定例外地從卡利基金撥付資金，該規定於該次會議結束時應停止適用，且不影響屆時將採納之分配方法論：<br />\n(a) 在開發中國家締約方之間，依據決議 16/2 附件第 18 段與第 20 段：<br />\n(i) [25%][20%] 平等分配予所有國家；<br />\n(ii) [25%][10%][20%] 依據經聯合國攤款比例公式所用因子調整後之每人國民總所得（GNI）進行分配；經調整後之每人 GNI 較低之國家將獲得較高分配；<br />\n(iii) [50%][70%][60%] 依據全球環境基金所採用之生物多樣性利益指數（更新自全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間之全球層級資料）進行分配；<br />\n(b) 在原住民族與地方社區之間，其分配額之 [90%] 預留予開發中國家之原住民族與地方社區，並依上述第 25 (a) 段於各國間進行分配，其分配額之 [10%] 預留予已開發國家之原住民族與地方社區。[在這些分配額中，資金得根據原住民族與地方社區自我認定的優先事項進行撥付，但須符合並受決議 16/2 附件所列安排之約束；]</p>"},{"md":"26. [**決定**依據已達成協議之方法論所進行之分配，應在第十八次締約方大會通過最終分配方法論後，視情況進行調整，以確保與最終方法論之一致；]","html":"<p>26. [<strong>決定</strong>依據已達成協議之方法論所進行之分配，應在第十八次締約方大會通過最終分配方法論後，視情況進行調整，以確保與最終方法論之一致；]</p>"},{"md":"27. **強調**分配方法論將隨著更多且新資訊的取得而隨時間演進，並**承認**該方法論需根據分配方法論特設技術專家小組之建議，進行進一步的技術開發與精煉；","html":"<p>27. <strong>強調</strong>分配方法論將隨著更多且新資訊的取得而隨時間演進，並<strong>承認</strong>該方法論需根據分配方法論特設技術專家小組之建議，進行進一步的技術開發與精煉；</p>"},{"md":"28. **請求**指導委員會依據第 25 段所述之分配方法論進行作業，且不預判其在第十八次締約方大會上之精煉結果；","html":"<p>28. <strong>請求</strong>指導委員會依據第 25 段所述之分配方法論進行作業，且不預判其在第十八次締約方大會上之精煉結果；</p>"},{"md":"29. **邀請**締約方就特設技術專家小組之報告以及第 25 段所述之分配方法論提交意見；","html":"<p>29. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方就特設技術專家小組之報告以及第 25 段所述之分配方法論提交意見；</p>"},{"md":"***\n³ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.","html":"<hr />\n<p>³ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.</p>"}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p005.md","en":"                                                                              CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n       30. Decides to establish, subject to the availability of resources, an Ad Hoc Technical\nExpert Group on Allocation Methodology with the terms of reference provided in annex I, taking\ninto account the views referred to in paragraph 29, and allowing for exchange of views between the\nAd Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology and the Steering Committee,\nspecifically to:\n       (a) Identify and evaluate new or updated data relevant to the allocation methodology, in\nparticular for the calculation of allocations to targeted governments, including data and indicators\ngenerated under the Convention and the Monitoring Framework of the Kunming-Montreal Global\nBiodiversity Framework;\n      (b) Develop a methodology specifically for the purpose of calculating allocations to\nindigenous peoples and local communities, with their full and effective participation in the process,\nincluding consideration of women and young people within those communities, including the\nassessment of the specific distributional effects of the interim and alternative approaches for them;\n       (c) Develop criterion (b) of the allocation methodology on the geographical origin of the\ngenetic resources from which digital sequence information on genetic resources in the database was\nderived, including potential recognized sources of data available at the global level, such as an\nindicator, and as applicable, the potential need to develop a new indicator, and in all cases reporting\non options for custodianship of the indicator, current or future availability, an assessment of biases\nand gaps, as well as a global evaluation of the need and feasibility to provide data for such a criterion;\n       (d) To provide information on its work pursuant to subparagraphs 30 (a), (b) and (c) for\nconsideration by the ad hoc open-ended working group and with a view to adopt the revised\nallocation methodology at the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n       31. Decides that to ensure the ability to disburse funds to indigenous peoples and local\ncommunities, the proposal from the Steering Committee consistent with paragraph 21 of the annex\nto decision 16/2, including, subject to national circumstances and national legislation, through\ngovernment authorities or by direct payments through institutions identified by indigenous peoples\nand local communities direct allocation through institutions identified by indigenous peoples and\nlocal communities themselves, national-level delivery through designated entities, and hybrid or\ncontext-specific arrangements, taking into account national circumstances and national legislation;\nII\nNon-monetary benefit sharing and data availability and accessibility\n       32. Recognises that further work is needed to operationalise the elements of the Multilateral\nMechanism that address non-monetary benefit sharing and capacity building and development,\nacknowledges the important role they play in the effective implementation of the Mechanism and\nnotes the need for adequate funding to support such activities, in line decision 16/2;\n      33.     Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to:\n      (a) Invite Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and\nrelevant organizations and stakeholders, in particular the scientific community, to share views,\ninformation, and on-going work on digital sequence information on genetic resources non-monetary\nbenefit-sharing including, inter alia, best practices, practical options for enhancing the delivery,\naccessibility and effectiveness of non-monetary benefits, particularly for developing country Parties,\nincluding least developed countries and small island developing States, projects and methods for\nquantifying and demonstrating non-monetary benefit-sharing;\n       (b) Commission a study, under the guidance of the Steering Committee, on current non-\nmonetary benefit-sharing by all users of digital sequence information on genetic resources in order\nto identify, inter alia:\n\n\n\n                                                                                                     5/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"30. **決定**在資源可用的情況下，根據附件 I 所提供的任務說明，成立一個關於分配方法論的特設技術專家小組，並考慮第 29 段所述之意見，並允許分配方法論特設技術專家小組與指導委員會之間進行意見交流，特別是為了：\n(a) 識別並評估與分配方法論相關的新型或更新之資料，特別是針對向目標政府分配額度之計算，包括在《公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》監測架構下所產生的資料與指標；\n(b) 開發一套專門用於計算向原住民族與地方社區分配額度之方法論，並確保其全面且有效地參與該過程，包括考量該社群內之女性與青年，以及評估其針對過渡性與替代性方法之特定分配影響；\n(c) 就資料庫中遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源地理來源，開發分配方法論之準則 (b)，包括全球層級可取得之潛在公認資料來源（例如指標），以及在適用情況下，開發新指標之潛在需求，且在所有情況下，皆須報告關於指標保管之選項、目前或未來之可用性、偏誤與差距之評估，以及對於提供該準則所需資料之需求與可行性的全球性評估；\n(d) 就其根據第 30 (a)、(b) 及 (c) 分段所進行之工作提供資訊，供特設開放式工作小組審議，並旨在於第十八次締約方大會時通過修訂後之分配方法論；","html":"<p>30. <strong>決定</strong>在資源可用的情況下，根據附件 I 所提供的任務說明，成立一個關於分配方法論的特設技術專家小組，並考慮第 29 段所述之意見，並允許分配方法論特設技術專家小組與指導委員會之間進行意見交流，特別是為了：<br />\n(a) 識別並評估與分配方法論相關的新型或更新之資料，特別是針對向目標政府分配額度之計算，包括在《公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》監測架構下所產生的資料與指標；<br />\n(b) 開發一套專門用於計算向原住民族與地方社區分配額度之方法論，並確保其全面且有效地參與該過程，包括考量該社群內之女性與青年，以及評估其針對過渡性與替代性方法之特定分配影響；<br />\n(c) 就資料庫中遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源地理來源，開發分配方法論之準則 (b)，包括全球層級可取得之潛在公認資料來源（例如指標），以及在適用情況下，開發新指標之潛在需求，且在所有情況下，皆須報告關於指標保管之選項、目前或未來之可用性、偏誤與差距之評估，以及對於提供該準則所需資料之需求與可行性的全球性評估；<br />\n(d) 就其根據第 30 (a)、(b) 及 (c) 分段所進行之工作提供資訊，供特設開放式工作小組審議，並旨在於第十八次締約方大會時通過修訂後之分配方法論；</p>"},{"md":"31. **決定**為確保能夠向原住民族與地方社區撥付資金，依決議 16/2 附件第 21 段所載之指導委員會提案（包括在符合國家情況與國家立法之前提下，透過政府機關，或透過原住民族與地方社區所指定之機構進行直接付款，透過原住民族與地方社區自身指定之機構進行直接分配，透過指定實體進行國家層級之交付，以及混合或因應具體情況之安排），並考量國家情況與國家立法；","html":"<p>31. <strong>決定</strong>為確保能夠向原住民族與地方社區撥付資金，依決議 16/2 附件第 21 段所載之指導委員會提案（包括在符合國家情況與國家立法之前提下，透過政府機關，或透過原住民族與地方社區所指定之機構進行直接付款，透過原住民族與地方社區自身指定之機構進行直接分配，透過指定實體進行國家層級之交付，以及混合或因應具體情況之安排），並考量國家情況與國家立法；</p>"},{"md":"II\n非貨幣性利益分享與資料之可用性及可取得性","html":"<p>II<br />\n非貨幣性利益分享與資料之可用性及可取得性</p>"},{"md":"32. **認識到**需要進一步的工作，以使處理非貨幣性利益分享、能力建構與發展之多邊機制要素具備可操作性；**承認**其在該機制有效執行中所扮演的重要角色；並**注意到**需要充足的資金以支持此類活動，且應與決議 16/2 保持一致；","html":"<p>32. <strong>認識到</strong>需要進一步的工作，以使處理非貨幣性利益分享、能力建構與發展之多邊機制要素具備可操作性；<strong>承認</strong>其在該機制有效執行中所扮演的重要角色；並<strong>注意到</strong>需要充足的資金以支持此類活動，且應與決議 16/2 保持一致；</p>"},{"md":"33. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>33. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>"},{"md":"(a) **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人（特別是科學界），分享關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊非貨幣性利益分享之意見、資訊及進行中之工作，包括但不限於：最佳實務、增進非貨幣性利益之交付、可取得性與有效性之務實選項（特別是針對開發中國家締約方，包括低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、以及量化與證明非貨幣性利益分享之專案與方法；\n(b) 在指導委員會之指導下，委託進行一項關於所有遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者目前非貨幣性利益分享情況之研究，旨在識別，包括但不限於：","html":"<p>(a) <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人（特別是科學界），分享關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊非貨幣性利益分享之意見、資訊及進行中之工作，包括但不限於：最佳實務、增進非貨幣性利益之交付、可取得性與有效性之務實選項（特別是針對開發中國家締約方，包括低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、以及量化與證明非貨幣性利益分享之專案與方法；<br />\n(b) 在指導委員會之指導下，委託進行一項關於所有遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者目前非貨幣性利益分享情況之研究，旨在識別，包括但不限於：</p>"}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p006.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n             (i)     capacity gaps in accessing, using and generating such digital sequence information,\n                     including needs for the development of sustained scientific and technological capacities,\n                     pathways for the self-assessment of capacity needs;\n             (ii)    methods to monitor and report non-monetary benefits;\n             (iii)   examples of the successful delivery of targeted non-monetary benefits, including\n                     through the network of regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation\n                     support centres;\n             (iv)    overview of whether and how the same issues are being considered under other\n                     international access and benefit sharing agreements with due consideration of capacity-\n                     building, technology transfer, scientific cooperation and the development of national\n                     capacities to generate, manage, access and utilize digital sequence information on\n                     genetic resources;\n             (v)     ways in which non-monetary benefit contributions from the Multilateral Mechanism can\n                     be integrated into reporting as part of the monitoring framework for the Kunming-\n                     Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;\n             (vi)    requirements and further work needed on the clearing house for the Multilateral\n                     Mechanism provided for in paragraph 8 of the annex to decision 16/2, including\n                     transparency and accountability in reporting non-monetary benefit sharing, and;\n             (vii) recommendations for the Steering Committee for further operationalization,\n                   recognizing that non-monetary benefit-sharing complements, and does not substitute\n                   for, monetary benefit-sharing through the Cali Fund under decision 16/2;\n               (c) Provide the Steering Committee with the outcome of the work described in\n       subparagraph 33 (a) and (b) above for its consideration with the aim to share its views and give\n       recommendations, and submit the outcomes of this work to the ad hoc open-ended working group\n       for its consideration;\nData accessibility and accountability\n              34. Invites, with the aim of making digital sequence information on genetic resources\n       publicly available and accessible in a transparent and accountable manner, consistent with the\n       sovereign rights of all Parties over the genetic resources and the rights of indigenous peoples and\n       local communities and consistent with the principles of open access to data:\n                      (a) Indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth among\n       them, to contribute, in consultation and collaboration, with Parties, and digital sequence information\n       on genetic resources database managers, the scientific community, users of digital sequence\n       information on genetic resources, relevant organizations and initiatives, as appropriate, to the\n       development of educational material for use by database operators, scientific and research\n       institutions, the Secretariat and other stakeholders, as relevant, on the management and governance\n       of data linked with indigenous peoples and local communities, including the women and youth within\n       those communities, and their traditional knowledge, including consideration of and alignment with\n       the principles of findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability (FAIR) and collective\n       benefit, authority to control, responsibility and ethics (CARE), and collective benefit, authority to\n       control, responsibility and ethics, and considering the recommendations set out in section III of the\n       United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization Recommendation on Open Science,\n       in order to, inter alia, providing guidance for scientific publications on research using digital\n       sequence information on genetic resources;\n                   (b) Organizations hosting databases that make digital sequence information on\n       genetic resources publicly available to share information with the Executive Secretary by the\n       eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties concerning their implementation of paragraph\n\n\n6/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"(i)","html":"<p>(i)</p>"},{"md":"取得、使用及產生此類數位序列資訊方面的能力差距，包括對於發展持續性科學與技術能力的需求，以及能力需求自我評估的路徑；","html":"<p>取得、使用及產生此類數位序列資訊方面的能力差距，包括對於發展持續性科學與技術能力的需求，以及能力需求自我評估的路徑；</p>"},{"md":"(ii)","html":"<p>(ii)</p>"},{"md":"監測與報告非貨幣利益的方法；","html":"<p>監測與報告非貨幣利益的方法；</p>"},{"md":"(iii)","html":"<p>(iii)</p>"},{"md":"成功達成特定非貨幣利益之範例，包括透過區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心網絡之方式；","html":"<p>成功達成特定非貨幣利益之範例，包括透過區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心網絡之方式；</p>"},{"md":"(iv)","html":"<p>(iv)</p>"},{"md":"概述在其他國際取得與利益分享協議下，是否以及如何考量相同議題，並應適當考慮到能力建構、技術轉移、科學合作，以及發展開發、管理、取得與利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之國家能力；","html":"<p>概述在其他國際取得與利益分享協議下，是否以及如何考量相同議題，並應適當考慮到能力建構、技術轉移、科學合作，以及發展開發、管理、取得與利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之國家能力；</p>"},{"md":"(v)","html":"<p>(v)</p>"},{"md":"將來自多邊機制之非貨幣利益貢獻，整合至昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之報告中之方式；","html":"<p>將來自多邊機制之非貨幣利益貢獻，整合至昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之報告中之方式；</p>"},{"md":"(vi)","html":"<p>(vi)</p>"},{"md":"針對決議 16/2 附件第 8 段所規定之多邊機制資訊交換所，所需之要求與進一步工作，包括非貨幣利益分享報告之透明度與問責制；以及","html":"<p>針對決議 16/2 附件第 8 段所規定之多邊機制資訊交換所，所需之要求與進一步工作，包括非貨幣利益分享報告之透明度與問責制；以及</p>"},{"md":"(vii)","html":"<p>(vii)</p>"},{"md":"針對指導委員會進一步運作化之建議，並承認非貨幣利益分享乃是對決議 16/2 下卡利基金貨幣利益分享之補充，而非取代；","html":"<p>針對指導委員會進一步運作化之建議，並承認非貨幣利益分享乃是對決議 16/2 下卡利基金貨幣利益分享之補充，而非取代；</p>"},{"md":"(c) 將上述第 33 (a) 及 (b) 小段所述工作之成果提供指導委員會審議，旨在分享其觀點並提出建議，並將此工作成果提交至特設開放式工作小組審議；","html":"<p>(c) 將上述第 33 (a) 及 (b) 小段所述工作之成果提供指導委員會審議，旨在分享其觀點並提出建議，並將此工作成果提交至特設開放式工作小組審議；</p>"},{"md":"資料可取得性與問責制","html":"<p>資料可取得性與問責制</p>"},{"md":"34. **邀請** 以使遺傳資源數位序列資訊能以透明且具問責制之方式公開且可取得，並符合所有締約方對遺傳資源之主權權利、原住民族與地方社區之權利，且符合資料開放取得原則為目標：","html":"<p>34. <strong>邀請</strong> 以使遺傳資源數位序列資訊能以透明且具問責制之方式公開且可取得，並符合所有締約方對遺傳資源之主權權利、原住民族與地方社區之權利，且符合資料開放取得原則為目標：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 原住民族與地方社區，包括其間之女性與青年，在與締約方、遺傳資源數位序列資訊資料庫管理員、科學界、遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者、相關組織與倡議（視情況適當）進行諮詢與合作之情況下，參與開發供資料庫營運者、科學與研究機構、秘書處及其他相關利害關係人使用之教育教材，內容涉及與原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）及其傳統知識相關之資料管理與治理，包括考量並符合可發現、可取得、可互操作與可重複使用（FAIR）以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理（CARE）之原則，並考量聯合國教育、科學及文化組織《科學開放建議書》第三節所列之建議，旨在（除其他事項外）為使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行研究之科學出版物提供指引；","html":"<p>(a) 原住民族與地方社區，包括其間之女性與青年，在與締約方、遺傳資源數位序列資訊資料庫管理員、科學界、遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者、相關組織與倡議（視情況適當）進行諮詢與合作之情況下，參與開發供資料庫營運者、科學與研究機構、秘書處及其他相關利害關係人使用之教育教材，內容涉及與原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）及其傳統知識相關之資料管理與治理，包括考量並符合可發現、可取得、可互操作與可重複使用（FAIR）以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理（CARE）之原則，並考量聯合國教育、科學及文化組織《科學開放建議書》第三節所列之建議，旨在（除其他事項外）為使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行研究之科學出版物提供指引；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 提供遺傳資源數位序列資訊公開取得之資料庫託管組織，於第十八次締約方大會召開前，就其執行","html":"<p>(b) 提供遺傳資源數位序列資訊公開取得之資料庫託管組織，於第十八次締約方大會召開前，就其執行</p>"}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p007.md","en":"                                                                                    CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n       10 of the annex to decision 16/2 while maintaining open access and taking into account existing\n       database practices;\n             35. Invites Parties and relevant organizations and stakeholders in a position to do so to\n       provide capacity-building, technical assistance, technology transfer and financial support for the\n       work outlined in subparagraphs 34 (a) and (b) above;]\n             36. Invites the various actors referred to in paragraph 34 above to inform the Secretariat of\n       relevant work undertaken and its results;\n              37.     Also requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:\n              (a) To collect the information mentioned in paragraph 36 above and disseminate it through\n       the clearing-house mechanism of the Convention and the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-\n       House;\n            (b) To issue a call for collaboration with other platforms and clearing houses outside the\n       Convention and its Protocols on the dissemination of that information;\n              38. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to ensure that\n       the findings and recommendations arising from the study on tools and models, such as databases, for\n       making digital sequence information on genetic resources publicly available and accessible in a\n       transparent and accountable manner4 are subject to peer review, allowing Parties, indigenous peoples\n       and local communities, database operators and relevant experts to provide comments, and to submit\n       the finalized study and recommendation for review by the Working Group;\n       III\n       Steering Committee and Governance of the Multilateral Mechanism\n              39. Welcomes the rule on the membership of the Steering Committee, including the\n       transitional arrangements for the staggered renewal of its current membership;5\n              40. Requests the Steering Committee to add a rule to their Rules of Procedure on members\n       selection stating that future members of the Steering Committee should be nominated by the\n       respective regional groups and constituencies, possessing appropriate qualifications related to access\n       and benefit sharing or finance, as determined by their nominating regional groups and constituencies,\n       so as to ensure the effective exercise of the functions of the Committee;\n             41. Requests the Executive Secretary to invite each region to nominate one representative\n       and to communicate the nomination through its respective Bureau member;\nStructured approach\n              42.      Takes note of the work of the Steering Committee on a structured approach to\n       implementation activities and, invites it, without prejudging ongoing discussions within the Steering\n       Committee on the operationalization of the Multilateral Mechanism or the outcomes of the\n       implementation on interim measures in this decision, and in accordance with decision 16/2, to\n       continue its work, generate evidence for the first review of the Multilateral Mechanism, including\n       results, conclusions and lessons learned from the structured approach, as applicable, and include the\n       outcomes of this work in the report and advice of the Steering Committee to the Conference of the\n       Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n             43.     Invites the Steering Committee to engage, as appropriate, with other actors that are\n       undertaking activities relevant to the structured approach to ensure complementary, and non-\n       duplicative approaches;\nOperational aspects of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund\n\n4 CBD/SBI/7/INF/15.\n5 CBD/COP/17/2 item 11 annex I\n\n\n\n                                                                                                         7/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"決議 16/2 附件第 10 段之情況，同時維持開放取得並考量現有的資料庫實務，與執行秘書分享資訊。\n35. 邀請締約方及有能力提供協助之相關組織與利害關係人，針對上述第 34 (a) 及 (b) 小段所述之工作，提供能力建構、技術協助、技術轉移與財務支持；]\n36. **邀請**上述第 34 段所述之各方參與者，將所進行之相關工作及其結果通報秘書處；\n37.","html":"<p>決議 16/2 附件第 10 段之情況，同時維持開放取得並考量現有的資料庫實務，與執行秘書分享資訊。<br />\n35. 邀請締約方及有能力提供協助之相關組織與利害關係人，針對上述第 34 (a) 及 (b) 小段所述之工作，提供能力建構、技術協助、技術轉移與財務支持；]<br />\n36. <strong>邀請</strong>上述第 34 段所述之各方參與者，將所進行之相關工作及其結果通報秘書處；<br />\n37.</p>"},{"md":"同時**請求**執行秘書，在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>同時<strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，在資源可用的情況下：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 收集上述第 36 段所述之資訊，並透過公約之資訊交換機制及取得與利益分享資訊交換所進行傳播；\n(b) 就該資訊之傳播，發出與公約及其議定書之外的其他平台與資訊交換所進行合作之呼籲；\n38. **請求**執行秘書，在資源可用的情況下，確保關於工具與模式（例如資料庫）之研究結果與建議——旨在以透明且負責任之方式，使遺傳資源數位序列資訊得以公開且可取得⁴——應經過同儕審查，並允許締約方、原住民族與地方社區、資料庫營運者及相關專家提供意見，並將完成之研究與建議提交予工作小組審查；","html":"<p>(a) 收集上述第 36 段所述之資訊，並透過公約之資訊交換機制及取得與利益分享資訊交換所進行傳播；<br />\n(b) 就該資訊之傳播，發出與公約及其議定書之外的其他平台與資訊交換所進行合作之呼籲；<br />\n38. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，在資源可用的情況下，確保關於工具與模式（例如資料庫）之研究結果與建議——旨在以透明且負責任之方式，使遺傳資源數位序列資訊得以公開且可取得⁴——應經過同儕審查，並允許締約方、原住民族與地方社區、資料庫營運者及相關專家提供意見，並將完成之研究與建議提交予工作小組審查；</p>"},{"md":"III\n多邊機制之指導委員會與治理","html":"<p>III<br />\n多邊機制之指導委員會與治理</p>"},{"md":"39. **歡迎**關於指導委員會成員資格之規則，包括其現有成員分階段更新之過渡安排；⁵\n40. **請求**指導委員會在其議事規則中增加一項關於成員遴選之規則，規定指導委員會之未來成員應由各自之區域集團與選民團提名，且須具備由其提名之區域集團與選民團所認定、與取得與利益分享或財務相關之適當資格，以確保委員會職能之有效行使；\n41. **請求**執行秘書邀請各區域提名一名代表，並透過其各自之主席團成員進行提名通報；","html":"<p>39. <strong>歡迎</strong>關於指導委員會成員資格之規則，包括其現有成員分階段更新之過渡安排；⁵<br />\n40. <strong>請求</strong>指導委員會在其議事規則中增加一項關於成員遴選之規則，規定指導委員會之未來成員應由各自之區域集團與選民團提名，且須具備由其提名之區域集團與選民團所認定、與取得與利益分享或財務相關之適當資格，以確保委員會職能之有效行使；<br />\n41. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書邀請各區域提名一名代表，並透過其各自之主席團成員進行提名通報；</p>"},{"md":"結構化方法","html":"<p>結構化方法</p>","pre":"透過其各自之主席團成員進行提名通報；\n\n"},{"md":"42. **注意到**指導委員會關於執行活動結構化方法之工作；且在不預判指導委員會內關於多邊機制運作化之進行中討論，或不預判本決議中關於臨時措施執行結果之情況下，並根據決議 16/2，**邀請**指導委員會繼續其工作，為多邊機制之首次審查產生證據，包括（視適用情況而定）結構化方法之結果、結論與經驗教訓，並將此項工作之成果納入指導委員會向第十八屆締約方大會提交之報告與建議中；\n43. **邀請**指導委員會在適當時與進行與結構化方法相關活動之其他參與者進行互動，以確保方法之互補性且不重複；","html":"<p>42. <strong>注意到</strong>指導委員會關於執行活動結構化方法之工作；且在不預判指導委員會內關於多邊機制運作化之進行中討論，或不預判本決議中關於臨時措施執行結果之情況下，並根據決議 16/2，<strong>邀請</strong>指導委員會繼續其工作，為多邊機制之首次審查產生證據，包括（視適用情況而定）結構化方法之結果、結論與經驗教訓，並將此項工作之成果納入指導委員會向第十八屆締約方大會提交之報告與建議中；<br />\n43. <strong>邀請</strong>指導委員會在適當時與進行與結構化方法相關活動之其他參與者進行互動，以確保方法之互補性且不重複；</p>"},{"md":"多邊機制之運作面向，包括卡利基金","html":"<p>多邊機制之運作面向，包括卡利基金</p>"},{"md":"⁴ CBD/SBI/7/INF/15。\n⁵ CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項附件 I","html":"<p>⁴ CBD/SBI/7/INF/15。<br />\n⁵ CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項附件 I</p>"},{"md":"7/11","html":"<p>7/11</p>"}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p008.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n\n\n             44. Recalls that the Multilateral Mechanism for the Fair and Equitable Benefit Sharing from\n       the Use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic Resources, including the Cali Fund, operates\n       under the authority and guidance of and is accountable to the Conference of Parties, in accordance\n       with decision 16/2;\n             45. Also recalls that the Cali Fund is currently administered by the United Nations through\n       the Multi-Partner Trust Fund Office, as foreseen in decisions of the Conference of Parties at its\n       sixteenth meeting;\n             46. Acknowledges that the ‘Standard Memorandum of Understanding to establish the\n       partnership between United Nations Organizations’ and to open a Fund administered by the Multi-\n       Partner Trust Fund of the United Nations contains language which sets the basis of this partnership\n       as agreed by the Members to the United Nations and approved by the UN Sustainable Development\n       Group, and that in consequence, some adjustments may be proposed to the text to ensure its\n       consistency with decision 16/2 and the authority and guidance of the Conference of the Parties over\n       the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;\n              47. Also acknowledges that the signatories of the Memorandum of Understanding of the\n       Cali Fund are the UNDP, the UNEP, and the SCBD, as an agreement with the MPTFO, and that the\n       legal and fiduciary responsibility that it engages is required to align with their established legal\n       framework;\n              48. Further acknowledges that the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, is to\n       be reviewed by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting, and that this review is\n       inclusive of governance of the Mechanism, including the Memorandum of Understanding, its\n       annexes and the Steering Committee’s terms of reference and modus operandi;\n               49. Considers that the Memorandum of Understanding of the Multilateral Mechanism and\n       its annexes, including the Cali Fund should align with decision 16/2 and decision 15/9 and that the\n       Memorandum of Understanding and its Annexes should reflect that the Cali Fund is a Fund to\n       facilitate monetary benefit-sharing from the use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic\n       Resources;\n             50. Therefore calls upon the signatories of the Memorandum of Understanding of the Cali\n       Fund to adjust terminology in the Memorandum of Understanding from donor/donations to\n       contributor/contributions, consistent with the benefit-sharing arrangements established under\n       decision 16/2;\n             51. Notes that the Steering Committee was convened for the first time only then after the\n       signature of the Memorandum of Understanding by the United Nations Partners and the Multi-\n       Partner Trust Fund Office;\n              [52. Decides to establish on an exceptional and time-bound basis, subject to the availability\n       of resources, a legal experts group with one member, with experience on similar agreements and\n       mechanisms, nominated by each UN region, and one from indigenous peoples and local\n       communities, according to the established procedures, with a mandate to examine, with the support\n       of the legal experts of United Nations Participating Organizations and the Multi-Partner Trust Fund\n       Office, [as well as an observer from the business sector], the language of the Memorandum of\n       Understanding including its annexes and the Steering Committee’s terms of reference and operations\n       manual, assess their optimal alignment with decision 16/2, and ,and to prepare recommendations for\n       further alignment including any clarifications, amendments or corrective measures, as applicable and\n       as necessary, to preserve the benefit-sharing nature of the Cali Fund, ensure transparency and\n       accountability, clarify institutional mandates and responsibilities,]\n             53. Also decides that this group shall meet online, subject to the availability of resources,\n       with additional online meetings as needed;\n\n8/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"44. **回顧**關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以實現公平且公正之利益分享的多邊機制（包括卡利基金），係根據決議 16/2，在締約方大會的權威與指導下運作，並對締約方大會負責；\n45. 亦**回顧**卡利基金目前由聯合國透過多方信託基金辦公室進行管理，正如締約方大會第十六次會議之決議所預見；\n46. **承認**「建立聯合國組織間夥伴關係之標準合作備忘錄」以及「透過聯合國多方信託基金開設基金」之內容，包含由聯合國會員國所同意並經聯合國永續發展集團批准之文字，奠定了此項夥伴關係之基礎；因此，可能需對文本提出若干調整，以確保其與決議 16/2 以及締約方大會對包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制所擁有的權威與指導地位保持一致；\n47. 亦**承認**卡利基金合作備忘錄之簽署方為聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）、聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）及生物多樣性公約秘書處（SCBD），此為與多方信託基金辦公室（MPTFO）簽署之協議；且其所承擔之法律與受託責任，必須與其既定之法律框架保持一致；\n48. 進一步**承認**締約方大會將於其第十八次會議對包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制進行審查，且此項審查應包含該機制之治理，包括合作備忘錄、其附件，以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作方式；\n49. **認為**多邊機制之合作備忘錄及其附件（包括卡利基金）應與決議 16/2 及決議 15/9 保持一致，且合作備忘錄及其附件應反映卡利基金係一旨在促進利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之金錢利益分享之基金；\n50. 因此，**呼籲**卡利基金合作備忘錄之簽署方調整合作備忘錄中之術語，將「捐贈者／捐贈」（donor/donations）改為「出資者／出資」（contributor/contributions），以與決議 16/2 下所建立之利益分享安排保持一致；\n51. **注意到**指導委員會僅在聯合國夥伴與多方信託基金辦公室簽署合作備忘錄之後，才首次召集；\n[52. **決定**在例外且有時限的情況下，在視資源可用性之情況下，依據既定程序，成立一個由一名成員組成的法律專家小組，成員由各聯合國區域提名，且具備類似協議與機制之經驗，並包含一名來自原住民族與地方社區之成員；其任務係在聯合國參與組織之法律專家及多方信託基金辦公室之支持下，[以及來自企業界之一名觀察員]，審查合作備忘錄（包括其附件）以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作手冊之文字，評估其與決議 16/2 之最佳一致性，並準備進一步一致化之建議，包括任何適用的且必要的澄清、修訂或糾正措施，以維護卡利基金之利益分享性質，確保透明度與問責制，並釐清機構職權與責任；]\n53. 亦**決定**在視資源可用性之情況下，此小組應進行線上會議，並根據需要增加額外的線上會議；","html":"<p>44. <strong>回顧</strong>關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以實現公平且公正之利益分享的多邊機制（包括卡利基金），係根據決議 16/2，在締約方大會的權威與指導下運作，並對締約方大會負責；<br />\n45. 亦<strong>回顧</strong>卡利基金目前由聯合國透過多方信託基金辦公室進行管理，正如締約方大會第十六次會議之決議所預見；<br />\n46. <strong>承認</strong>「建立聯合國組織間夥伴關係之標準合作備忘錄」以及「透過聯合國多方信託基金開設基金」之內容，包含由聯合國會員國所同意並經聯合國永續發展集團批准之文字，奠定了此項夥伴關係之基礎；因此，可能需對文本提出若干調整，以確保其與決議 16/2 以及締約方大會對包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制所擁有的權威與指導地位保持一致；<br />\n47. 亦<strong>承認</strong>卡利基金合作備忘錄之簽署方為聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）、聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）及生物多樣性公約秘書處（SCBD），此為與多方信託基金辦公室（MPTFO）簽署之協議；且其所承擔之法律與受託責任，必須與其既定之法律框架保持一致；<br />\n48. 進一步<strong>承認</strong>締約方大會將於其第十八次會議對包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制進行審查，且此項審查應包含該機制之治理，包括合作備忘錄、其附件，以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作方式；<br />\n49. <strong>認為</strong>多邊機制之合作備忘錄及其附件（包括卡利基金）應與決議 16/2 及決議 15/9 保持一致，且合作備忘錄及其附件應反映卡利基金係一旨在促進利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之金錢利益分享之基金；<br />\n50. 因此，<strong>呼籲</strong>卡利基金合作備忘錄之簽署方調整合作備忘錄中之術語，將「捐贈者／捐贈」（donor/donations）改為「出資者／出資」（contributor/contributions），以與決議 16/2 下所建立之利益分享安排保持一致；<br />\n51. <strong>注意到</strong>指導委員會僅在聯合國夥伴與多方信託基金辦公室簽署合作備忘錄之後，才首次召集；<br />\n[52. <strong>決定</strong>在例外且有時限的情況下，在視資源可用性之情況下，依據既定程序，成立一個由一名成員組成的法律專家小組，成員由各聯合國區域提名，且具備類似協議與機制之經驗，並包含一名來自原住民族與地方社區之成員；其任務係在聯合國參與組織之法律專家及多方信託基金辦公室之支持下，[以及來自企業界之一名觀察員]，審查合作備忘錄（包括其附件）以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作手冊之文字，評估其與決議 16/2 之最佳一致性，並準備進一步一致化之建議，包括任何適用的且必要的澄清、修訂或糾正措施，以維護卡利基金之利益分享性質，確保透明度與問責制，並釐清機構職權與責任；]<br />\n53. 亦<strong>決定</strong>在視資源可用性之情況下，此小組應進行線上會議，並根據需要增加額外的線上會議；</p>"}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p009.md","en":"                                                                                   CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n              54.    Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to:\n              (a)    Facilitate the formation of this group through a call for nomination;\n              (b)    Support this group in its work according to the mandate in paragraph 52;\n            (c) Report the outcomes of this work to the Steering Committee of the Multilateral\n       Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, for its technical review and comments, without prejudice to the\n       recommendations of the legal experts group;\n             (d) Communicates the report of the group and the outcomes of the review of the Steering\n       Committee to the ad hoc open-ended working group for their consideration [and] with a view to make\n       a recommendation to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting for its consideration and\n       approval, as appropriate;\n             55. Considers that in order for the good functioning and capitalization of the Multilateral\n       Mechanism including the Cali Fund, the Memorandum of Understanding as is currently drafted will\n       continue to apply and the contributors will be duly informed about the ongoing process on MOU\n       pursuant to this decision and that provisions of the MOU may be altered modifying any rights that\n       may be arising pursuant to the MOU;\n               56. Also decides that the Steering Committee may make modifications to operational\n       documents other than the Memorandum of Understanding in the event that it is needed to ensure their\n       responsibilities in the functioning of the Multilateral Mechanism, in particular not to delay the\n       capitalization of the Fund, such as a structural approach, provided that such modifications do not\n       alter the governance arrangements established under decision 16/2, without prejudice to the outcome\n       of the work of the Legal Expert Group;\n\n\n       IV\n       Review methodology\n              57. Decides to implement the review methodology6 for the purpose of the first review of\n       effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and with a view for this\n       methodology to be revised before the second review of effectiveness;\n             58. Requests that the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Steering Committee, in\n       line with the review methodology and subject to the availability of resources to:\n              (a) Develop and disseminate a survey available in all official languages of the United\n       Nations to collect relevant data and information from Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples\n       and local communities, women and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders and\n       organizations, including the scientific community, database managers and the private sector, in order\n       to inform the first review of the effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund,\n       and the development of surveys for future reviews;\n              (b)    Commission a review report containing:\n              (i)    an analysis of data and information submitted pursuant to subparagraph 58 (a) above\n                     that is in line with the pillars and governance assessment of the Multilateral Mechanism,\n                     including the Cali Fund, information from the global report on collective progress in the\n                     implementation of the Framework and other readily available sources, as relevant; and\n              (ii)   recommendations for improving the effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism,\n                     including the Cali Fund;\n\n\n\n6 CBD/COP/17/2 item 11 annex III\n\n\n\n                                                                                                         9/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"54.","html":"<p>54.</p>"},{"md":"**請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p><strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 透過徵求提名，促進本小組之成立；","html":"<p>(a) 透過徵求提名，促進本小組之成立；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 根據第 52 段之授權，支援本小組之工作；","html":"<p>(b) 根據第 52 段之授權，支援本小組之工作；</p>"},{"md":"(c) 將本工作之成果提交予包含卡利基金在內的多邊機制指導委員會，以進行其技術審查與評論，且不損害法律專家小組之建議；","html":"<p>(c) 將本工作之成果提交予包含卡利基金在內的多邊機制指導委員會，以進行其技術審查與評論，且不損害法律專家小組之建議；</p>"},{"md":"(d) 將本小組之報告及指導委員會之審查結果，提交予該特設開放式工作小組以供其審議[且]旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議，以供其審議與核准（視情況而定）；","html":"<p>(d) 將本小組之報告及指導委員會之審查結果，提交予該特設開放式工作小組以供其審議[且]旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議，以供其審議與核准（視情況而定）；</p>"},{"md":"55. **認為**為了使包含卡利基金在內的多邊機制能良好運作並完成注資，目前草擬之諒解備忘錄應繼續適用，且貢獻者應根據本決議，就諒解備忘錄之進行中程序獲得適當通知，且諒解備忘錄之條款得進行變更，並修改任何可能根據諒解備忘錄而產生之權利；","html":"<p>55. <strong>認為</strong>為了使包含卡利基金在內的多邊機制能良好運作並完成注資，目前草擬之諒解備忘錄應繼續適用，且貢獻者應根據本決議，就諒解備忘錄之進行中程序獲得適當通知，且諒解備忘錄之條款得進行變更，並修改任何可能根據諒解備忘錄而產生之權利；</p>"},{"md":"56. **亦決定**指導委員會在必要時，得對諒解備忘錄以外之作業文件進行修改，以確保其在多邊機制運作中之職責（特別是為了不延誤基金之注資，例如結構性方法），惟此類修改不得改變根據決議 16/2 所建立之治理安排，且不損害法律專家小組工作之結果；","html":"<p>56. <strong>亦決定</strong>指導委員會在必要時，得對諒解備忘錄以外之作業文件進行修改，以確保其在多邊機制運作中之職責（特別是為了不延誤基金之注資，例如結構性方法），惟此類修改不得改變根據決議 16/2 所建立之治理安排，且不損害法律專家小組工作之結果；</p>"},{"md":"IV\n審查方法論","html":"<p>IV<br />\n審查方法論</p>"},{"md":"57. **決定**實施審查方法論⁶，旨在對包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制進行首次有效性審查，並預期此方法論應在第二次有效性審查前進行修訂；","html":"<p>57. <strong>決定</strong>實施審查方法論⁶，旨在對包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制進行首次有效性審查，並預期此方法論應在第二次有效性審查前進行修訂；</p>"},{"md":"58. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢指導委員會、符合審查方法論且在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>58. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢指導委員會、符合審查方法論且在資源可用的情況下：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 開發並發布一份以聯合國所有官方語言呈現之問卷，以從締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織，以及其他相關利害關係人與組織（包括科學界、資料庫管理員及私營部門）蒐集相關資料與資訊，以作為包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制首次有效性審查及未來審查問卷開發之參考；","html":"<p>(a) 開發並發布一份以聯合國所有官方語言呈現之問卷，以從締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織，以及其他相關利害關係人與組織（包括科學界、資料庫管理員及私營部門）蒐集相關資料與資訊，以作為包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制首次有效性審查及未來審查問卷開發之參考；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 委託編製一份審查報告，其中包含：","html":"<p>(b) 委託編製一份審查報告，其中包含：</p>"},{"md":"(i) 針對根據上述第 58 (a) 小段所提交之資料與資訊進行分析，且該分析應與包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制支柱與治理評估相符，並結合關於綱要實施集體進展之全球報告資訊及其他相關之易取得來源；以及","html":"<p>(i) 針對根據上述第 58 (a) 小段所提交之資料與資訊進行分析，且該分析應與包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制支柱與治理評估相符，並結合關於綱要實施集體進展之全球報告資訊及其他相關之易取得來源；以及</p>"},{"md":"(ii) 旨在提升包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制有效性之建議；","html":"<p>(ii) 旨在提升包含卡利基金在內之多邊機制有效性之建議；</p>"},{"md":"---\n⁶ CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項目附件 III","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁶ CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項目附件 III</p>"}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p010.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n               (c) Submit the review report to the Steering Committee to give it the opportunity to share\n        its views and give any recommendations that it may have thereon, and submit the report and the\n        recommendations of the ad hoc open-ended working group;\n              59.      Invites the actors concerned to respond to the survey mentioned in subparagraph 58 (a)\n        above;\n             60. Requests that the working group review the report as well as any comments or\n        recommendations of the Steering Committee on such report;\n        V\n        Support for the operationalization of the Mechanism\n              61. Calls upon Parties with users in their jurisdiction to take measures to ensure that users\n        contribute to the global fund in line with the modalities of the Multilateral Mechanism, as appropriate\n        within their national context in accordance with decision 16/2;\n              62. Calls upon Parties, and invites other Governments, relevant organizations and\n        stakeholders, including the private sector, to organize participatory activities and partnerships, as\n        appropriate, in order to encourage private sector engagement with and contributions to the Cali Fund\n        and non-monetary benefit-sharing consistent with decision 16/2;\n               63. Requests Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations, to support\n        the work of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and the\n        Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity 7 acting as the interim Secretariat of the\n        Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, through financial support and formal and informal activities,\n        [including through capacity-building, technical assistance, awareness-raising and information-\n        sharing,] such as workshops on the operationalization of the Mechanism, including the Cali Fund,\n        and related items to continue supporting the effective participation in the work of the Committee of\n        members from developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small\n        island developing States among them;\n              64. Requests the Executive Secretary to enhance cooperation with the Secretariats of other\n        relevant international organizations and bodies, such as the International Treaty on Plant Genetic\n        Resources for Food and Agriculture, the World Health Organization, the World International\n        Property Organization, and the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the\n        Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond\n        National Jurisdiction to promote mutual supportiveness and synergies in order to address common\n        challenges;\n\nAnnex I\nTerms of reference for the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation\nMethodology\n        1     The Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology is to provide technical advice\n        and guidance on the allocation methodology(ies) for disbursing funding, as decided in the annex to\n        decision 16/2 from the global fund, to:\n                 (a) governments in developing country Parties (paragraph 18 of the annex to decision 16/2),\n                     on the basis of the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation\n                     Methodology8 and taking into consideration the recommendations for future work;\n                 (b) indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth within those\n                     communities (paragraph 21 of the annex to decision 16/2), on the basis of the report\n7 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n8 CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3\n\n\n\n10/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"(c) 將審查報告提交至指導委員會，以使其有機會分享其意見並提出任何其可能對此所提出的建議，並提交該特設開放式工作小組之報告與建議；\n59. **邀請**相關參與者回應第 58 (a) 小段所述之調查；","html":"<p>(c) 將審查報告提交至指導委員會，以使其有機會分享其意見並提出任何其可能對此所提出的建議，並提交該特設開放式工作小組之報告與建議；<br />\n59. <strong>邀請</strong>相關參與者回應第 58 (a) 小段所述之調查；</p>"},{"md":"60. **請求**工作小組審查該報告以及指導委員會對該報告之任何評論或建議；","html":"<p>60. <strong>請求</strong>工作小組審查該報告以及指導委員會對該報告之任何評論或建議；</p>"},{"md":"V\n對機制運作之支持\n61. **呼籲**在其管轄範圍內設有使用者的締約方，採取適當措施，確保使用者根據其國家情境，並依照決議 16/2，依據多邊機制之模式為全球基金做出貢獻；\n62. **呼籲**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、相關組織與利害關係人（包括私營部門），在適當情況下組織參與式活動與夥伴關係，以鼓勵私營部門參與並對卡利基金及非貨幣性利益分享做出貢獻，且須與決議 16/2 一致；\n63. **請求**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府與相關組織，透過財務支持以及正式與非正式活動，支持多邊機制指導委員會（包括卡利基金）以及擔任該機制（包括卡利基金）臨時秘書處之生物多樣性公約秘書處之工作，[包括透過能力建構、技術援助、提升意識與資訊分享，] 例如關於機制（包括卡利基金）運作之工作坊及相關項目，以持續支持開發中國家締約方成員（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）有效參與委員會之工作；\n64. **請求**執行秘書加強與其他相關國際組織與機構之合作，例如《糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約》、世界衛生組織、世界智慧財產權組織，以及《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用之協議，以促進相互支持與綜效，從而應對共同挑戰；","html":"<p>V<br />\n對機制運作之支持<br />\n61. <strong>呼籲</strong>在其管轄範圍內設有使用者的締約方，採取適當措施，確保使用者根據其國家情境，並依照決議 16/2，依據多邊機制之模式為全球基金做出貢獻；<br />\n62. <strong>呼籲</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、相關組織與利害關係人（包括私營部門），在適當情況下組織參與式活動與夥伴關係，以鼓勵私營部門參與並對卡利基金及非貨幣性利益分享做出貢獻，且須與決議 16/2 一致；<br />\n63. <strong>請求</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府與相關組織，透過財務支持以及正式與非正式活動，支持多邊機制指導委員會（包括卡利基金）以及擔任該機制（包括卡利基金）臨時秘書處之生物多樣性公約秘書處之工作，[包括透過能力建構、技術援助、提升意識與資訊分享，] 例如關於機制（包括卡利基金）運作之工作坊及相關項目，以持續支持開發中國家締約方成員（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）有效參與委員會之工作；<br />\n64. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書加強與其他相關國際組織與機構之合作，例如《糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約》、世界衛生組織、世界智慧財產權組織，以及《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用之協議，以促進相互支持與綜效，從而應對共同挑戰；</p>"},{"md":"附件 I\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組職權範圍\n1\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組應針對從全球基金撥付資金之分配方法論，提供技術建議與指導，其內容如決議 16/2 附件所定，對象包括：\n(a) 開發中國家締約方之政府（決議 16/2 附件第 18 段），其基礎為分配方法論特設技術專家小組之工作，並考量未來工作之建議；\n(b) 原住民族與地方社區，包括該社區內之女性與青年（決議 16/2 附件第 21 段），其基礎為報告","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組職權範圍<br />\n1<br />\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組應針對從全球基金撥付資金之分配方法論，提供技術建議與指導，其內容如決議 16/2 附件所定，對象包括：<br />\n(a) 開發中國家締約方之政府（決議 16/2 附件第 18 段），其基礎為分配方法論特設技術專家小組之工作，並考量未來工作之建議；<br />\n(b) 原住民族與地方社區，包括該社區內之女性與青年（決議 16/2 附件第 21 段），其基礎為報告</p>"},{"md":"---\n7 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n8 CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3","html":"<hr />\n<p>7 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.<br />\n8 CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3</p>"},{"md":"10/11","html":"<p>10/11</p>"}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4184e060f9fe69e17a69e/p011.md","en":"                                                                              CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19\n\n             mentioned above as well as other relevant sources, including discussions with the\n             Steering Committee;\n2.    The Group is to submit its report to the ad hoc open-ended working group, with the view to\nmake recommendations to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n3.     The Technical Expert Group will comprise technical experts, as follows: 15 nominated by\nParties, 7 nominated by representatives of indigenous peoples and local communities from the seven\nsociocultural regions, and 4 nominated by relevant organizations. The Executive Secretary, in\nconsultation with the Bureau, will select experts on the basis of nominations received, taking gender\nand the relevant technical expertise of the candidates into account and applying the procedure for\navoiding or managing conflicts of interest set out in the annex to decision 14/33, as amended in\ndecision 16/26.\n4     The Technical Expert Group may draw on existing expertise and liaise with relevant\norganizations, as appropriate, in the execution of its mandate.\n5    The Technical Expert Group may consider, inter alia, the following:\n       (a) With regard to criterion (a), develop an indicator specifically addressing species richness\nand biodiversity, taking into account biological diversity; territorial extent and the extent of natural\necosystems; ecosystem diversity, including ecological distinctiveness; endemism; ecological\nintegrity and connectivity; and biodiversity conserved and sustainably used by Indigenous Peoples\nand local communities, including in their lands and territories;\n      (b) With regard to criterion (b), reformulate the indicator to clearly reflect the country of origin\nof the genetic resources from which the digital sequence information on genetic resources was\nderived, rather than the country in which the digital sequence information on genetic resources was\ngenerated or uploaded to a database;\n       (c) With regard to criterion (c), develop an indicator based on information available in National\nBiodiversity Strategies and Action Plans (NBSAPs) and national capacity-development plans,\nreflecting capacity needs for the conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity, taking into account\nthe circumstances of developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small\nisland developing States, Parties with economies in transition, megadiverse developing country\nParties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, Parties with\neconomies in transition, megadiverse developing countries, and the needs of indigenous peoples and\nlocal communities, while avoiding indicators that merely reflect the economic development or\npayment capacity of Parties.\n\n6.    Subject to the availability of financial resources, the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group will\nmeet, as needed, to ensure the timely provision of advice and, wherever possible, back-to-back with\nother relevant meetings. Where possible, the Secretariat will use available means of electronic\ncommunication to reduce the need for in-person meetings._\n                                              __________\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                    11/11","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.19</p>"},{"md":"如上所述以及其他相關來源，包括與指導委員會的討論；\n2.\n該小組應向特設開放式工作小組提交其報告，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；\n3.\n技術專家小組將由技術專家組成，如下：15 名由締約方提名，7 名由來自七個社會文化區域的原住民族與地方社區代表提名，以及 4 名由相關組織提名。執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，根據收到的提名，在考慮候選人之性別及相關技術專業，並適用決議 14/33 附件（經決議 16/26 修訂）所規定之避免或管理利益衝突程序之基礎上，選任專家。\n4.\n技術專家小組在執行其職責時，得視情況利用現有專業知識並與相關組織保持聯繫。\n5.\n技術專家小組可考慮，除其他事項外，下列事項：","html":"<p>如上所述以及其他相關來源，包括與指導委員會的討論；<br />\n2.<br />\n該小組應向特設開放式工作小組提交其報告，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；<br />\n3.<br />\n技術專家小組將由技術專家組成，如下：15 名由締約方提名，7 名由來自七個社會文化區域的原住民族與地方社區代表提名，以及 4 名由相關組織提名。執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，根據收到的提名，在考慮候選人之性別及相關技術專業，並適用決議 14/33 附件（經決議 16/26 修訂）所規定之避免或管理利益衝突程序之基礎上，選任專家。<br />\n4.<br />\n技術專家小組在執行其職責時，得視情況利用現有專業知識並與相關組織保持聯繫。<br />\n5.<br />\n技術專家小組可考慮，除其他事項外，下列事項：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 關於準則 (a)，開發一個專門針對物種豐富度與生物多樣性的指標，並考量生物多樣性；領土範圍與自然生態系範圍；生態系多樣性，包括生態獨特性；特有種；生態完整性與連結性；以及由原住民族與地方社區在其土地與領土內所保育及永續利用之生物多樣性；\n(b) 關於準則 (b)，重新制定指標，以清楚反映遺傳資源之來源國（即遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國），而非產生或上傳至資料庫之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所在之國家；\n(c) 關於準則 (c)，開發一個基於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs) 及國家能力建構計畫中可用資訊之指標，以反映生物多樣性保育與永續利用之能力需求，並考量開發中國家締約方之情況，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極其豐富之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極其豐富之開發中國家，以及原住民族與地方社區之需求，同時避免僅反映締約方經濟發展或支付能力之指標。\n6.\n在財務資源可用之情況下，特設技術專家小組將根據需要進行會議，以確保及時提供建議，並在可能的情況下，與其他相關會議接續舉行。在可能的情況下，秘書處將利用現有的電子通訊手段，以減少實體會議之需求。","html":"<p>(a) 關於準則 (a)，開發一個專門針對物種豐富度與生物多樣性的指標，並考量生物多樣性；領土範圍與自然生態系範圍；生態系多樣性，包括生態獨特性；特有種；生態完整性與連結性；以及由原住民族與地方社區在其土地與領土內所保育及永續利用之生物多樣性；<br />\n(b) 關於準則 (b)，重新制定指標，以清楚反映遺傳資源之來源國（即遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國），而非產生或上傳至資料庫之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所在之國家；<br />\n(c) 關於準則 (c)，開發一個基於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs) 及國家能力建構計畫中可用資訊之指標，以反映生物多樣性保育與永續利用之能力需求，並考量開發中國家締約方之情況，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極其豐富之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極其豐富之開發中國家，以及原住民族與地方社區之需求，同時避免僅反映締約方經濟發展或支付能力之指標。<br />\n6.<br />\n在財務資源可用之情況下，特設技術專家小組將根據需要進行會議，以確保及時提供建議，並在可能的情況下，與其他相關會議接續舉行。在可能的情況下，秘書處將利用現有的電子通訊手段，以減少實體會議之需求。</p>"}]}]};
